  "description": "Which Broad Rental Market Area (BRMA) supplies the rent figures for each council area in Scotland and local government district in Northern Ireland. ONS publishes private rents for these two nations by BRMA, not by local authority.",
  "method": "Each council takes the BRMA that ONS names as its best match on its 'Housing prices in your area' page: the BRMA containing the largest share of the council's postcodes (ONS ignores overlaps under 1% of postcodes). In Scotland ONS assigns each council area to exactly one BRMA. In Northern Ireland BRMAs are built from postcode districts and several councils overlap more than one; the other overlapping BRMAs are listed under overlaps. The brief asks for the BRMA covering most of the population; the share of postcodes is the closest published measure, and no BRMA population split is published.",
  "source": {
    "title": "ONS, Housing prices in your area (local authority pages, rents section)",
